  "summary": {
    "kind": "quote",
    "span": {
      "end": 2126,
      "end_line": 28,
      "line": 28,
      "start": 1712
    },
    "text": "The orchestrator briefs models outside Delphi in two ways: it dispatches to external CLI seats, and it advises host models through `consult_orchestrator` and `spawn_agent_pack`. Inside Delphi, a handoff is checked and a gate decides the outcome. Outside, neither holds. This spec makes outside briefs carry what the orchestrator needs in order to tell whether the work is done, without widening anyone's authority."
  }
